       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. The usual limit is 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with that note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
