       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave doesn't explain the dose. Family visiting and wanting things settled before rounds don't justify 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen. That is double the maximum daily dose, and it carries a real risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. I can't see a clinical context that makes it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf I've misread the situation and there's a specific clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a consult recommendation, tell me what it is. Even then, I'd suggest running it by pharmacy first. If you decide to place it yourself, you can enter it directly in the order system, where pharmacy verification will also review it.\n\nIf the goal is better pain control or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a scheduled adjunct instead, such as acetaminophen. Tell me which option you'd like."
      }
